  "prompt": "You receive 5 images. Image 1 is the LAYOUT SKETCH of the finished 1920x1080 game screen: a crude flat-colour blocking that fixes the exact composition - camera, horizon, wall and floor lines, and the position, size and outline of every object. Repaint image 1 into a finished painting: keep every line and every block exactly where it is and exactly as large as it is, paint each block as the object described below, do not move, enlarge, shrink, add or remove anything, and leave no flat colour areas or hard geometric edges. Images 2-4 are photos of the real place (geography, architecture, materials and real details to paint from; they are references only, do not copy their camera, cars, people, signs or weather). Image 5 is a finished background painting from our game: use it ONLY as the reference for the painting technique (brushwork, palette, edge softness, level of detail, line quality); do not copy anything from its scene.\n\nPlace: the main entrance of the primary school ZS Sokolikova 2 (built 1974) in Bratislava-Dubravka, Slovakia, on its long two-storey south-west facade, seen from the paved forecourt in front of it. Images 2 and 3 are photos of this real entrance (2016): the long facade with ribbon windows on both floors above a low plinth, the glazed entrance doors under a projecting canopy, the landing with a few steps, the ramp with a railing rising along the facade, small concrete planters, the forecourt path. Image 4 is our own earlier painting of the same entrance: use it for the mood, the canopy, steps, ramp and planters. In both, the white PVC windows, the grey mosaic panels and the newer canopy are the later state; paint the school as it was in 1995.\n\nBrief: the school in June 1995 on a sunny afternoon: warm afternoon sunlight from the left, falling straight onto the facade, soft dappled shadows of the big trees behind the camera on the forecourt, fresh green leaves. The building is 21 years old: the wall panels of the whole facade (the plinth, the bands between the window ribbons and the wall around the entrance) are ONE SINGLE plain warm pale-yellow colour - no murals, no mosaic patterns, no graffiti; the original 1970s windows: white-painted timber double windows divided into tall casements with small upper hoppers, a few hoppers tilted open; an older canopy over the entrance (thin grey steel frame, corrugated wired-glass roof) on two slim posts. Above the canopy a white enamel name board with dark blue capital letters in two lines: ZÁKLADNÁ ŠKOLA / SOKOLÍKOVA, with a small round blue school crest at its left end (a stylised open book with a little bird, no text). A functioning afternoon school: one hopper window open, a glazed notice board of the afternoon club at the left.\n\nCamera: eye level 1.74 m above the forecourt, horizon at y 490; the facade is about 10 m away and recedes gently to the right; vertical lines stay vertical. Keep this exact geometry from the sketch: the foot of the facade from y 750 at the left edge to y 671 at the building corner (x 1793), the ground-floor window ribbon from y ~320-390 down to its sill line at y ~600-640, the band between the floors, the upper-floor windows cut by the top edge, the entrance doors at x 897-1254 with their threshold at y ~650, the steps' front edge at y 755 between x 869 and 1356, the canopy's front edge at y 275-300, the building corner at x 1793 with the school yard beyond it.\n\nWhat the sketch blocks are, left to right: tree crowns from the lawn slope behind the camera hanging into the top-left and top-right corners; the long facade with its two ribbons of windows; the club notice board on two legs at the left on the forecourt; the ramp with a steel railing rising along the facade from the left to the entrance landing; the concrete planter at the foot of the steps; the entrance: landing, three steps, glazed double doors with side lights, canopy on two posts, the name board above it; further right more ground-floor windows, the last one before the corner being the caretaker's service window with a protruding light stone sill; the building corner; beyond it the school yard: lawn, lindens, a wire-mesh fence, panel blocks far away and a bit of blue sky; the paved forecourt along the whole bottom.\n\nInteractive props - each painted clearly inside its block, the same size as its block, easy to recognise at a glance:\n1. the block of the layout sketch at x 56-268, y 440-626 of the 1920x1080 frame (3-14 % from the left, 41-58 % from the top): a glazed notice board in a brown timber frame on two black metal legs, behind the glass colourful paper notices pinned up; the largest notice shows a hand-drawn reel-to-reel tape recorder with music notes (no readable text).\n2. the block of the layout sketch at x 712-838, y 668-768 of the 1920x1080 frame (37-44 % from the left, 62-71 % from the top): a square concrete planter cube with red geraniums, standing on the forecourt at the foot of the steps.\n3. the block of the layout sketch at x 893-1259, y 192-286 of the 1920x1080 frame (47-66 % from the left, 18-26 % from the top): the white enamel name board with the dark blue capitals ZÁKLADNÁ ŠKOLA / SOKOLÍKOVA and the small round blue school crest at its left end.\nthe area of the layout sketch at x 897-1254, y 362-653 of the 1920x1080 frame (47-65 % from the left, 34-60 % from the top) is the glazed entrance doors at the top of the steps. The forecourt path leaves the picture at the left edge (the area of the layout sketch at x 0-62, y 790-1015 of the 1920x1080 frame (0-3 % from the left, 73-94 % from the top)) and continues past the building corner to the school yard at the right edge (the area of the layout sketch at x 1830-1920, y 600-930 of the 1920x1080 frame (95-100 % from the left, 56-86 % from the top)).\n\nWalkable floor: the band at x 0-1920, y 686-1015 of the 1920x1080 frame (0-100 % from the left, 64-94 % from the top) is the open paved forecourt (grey concrete slabs) - one continuous flat surface with no kerb, step, edge or change of material inside it, and nothing standing on it: no bins, no benches, no bicycles, no bags, no people. Only sunlight, dappled leaf shadows and fine joints. The steps, the ramp, the planter and the notice board stand behind it, exactly as in the sketch.\nThis room has no NPC zones.\nFixed architectural anchor 'building_corner' at x 1793, y 400. Fixed architectural anchor 'entrance' at x 1082, y 647. Fixed architectural anchor 'planter' at x 775, y 715. Fixed architectural anchor 'service_window_visible_at_edge' at x 1681, y 470.\n\nFiction rules: the real school name may appear on the name board as asked; no other readable text, no real posters, no current school logo, no state emblem in 1995, no house numbers, no brand lettering. No people, no animals. Any paper shows only illegible scribbles, no digits.\n\nThe layout sketch is a blocking aid only: paint over all of it. Do NOT draw frames, borders, outlines or boxes around objects, and keep no flat colour block. The finished picture contains no UI, no captions, no text except what is asked for above, no watermark and no people or animals unless stated above.\n\nStyle: classic 1990s hand-painted adventure game background. Rich painterly brushwork, slightly exaggerated cartoon proportions with gently curved lines, warm late-afternoon sunlight, saturated but harmonious colours, soft dappled shadows under the trees.",
